Well, 957 days after playing NetHack for the first time, I finally won the
wretched thing.  I got Zeppo the Valkyrie out with the Amulet on my Amiga last
night.  Score? 1473932 points.  Other stats: pretty impressive, but you've all
seen those lists before so I'll leave it out.

My thanks to the Dev Team for what I have no hesitation in telling non-hackers
is my all-time favourite computer game, NetHack.  Thanks also to all those
who've posted anything to rec.games.hack over the years, making the game take
on a "more than just a game" type aura.

Now, having completed the game, I feel I'm in a position to make some
observations.

***** Possible Spoilers *****

1. Polypiling makes things rather _easy_.  When you get your AC to -48, and have
4 amulets of life-saving, every sort of ring,... you don't have too many
worries.  (Please note: This is NOT meant to re-kindle the Polypiling Flame
Wars in rec.games.hack, it's just an observation from one who used up a dozen
wands of polymorph on the one polypile.)

2. Paralyzing the Wiz before killing him, polymorphing into a nymph,
pick-pocketing the Amulet from him, and leaving the level before he starts
moving again makes for a boring climb back to the top.  It's probably worth
killing the Wiz just to have him reappearing on your way back to the top and
making things slightly more interesting.

Bye Now!
